From 0ce881a28c0afba10ab1b7da8f649c8f372515d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 06:18:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a park on the card's own orchestrator wakes
 that chat

t_9791ec808c66123a parked for a week (2026-11-18 22:25Z) "awaiting the owning
orchestrator's three decisions", declared as awaiting={kind:'external',
ref:'Owning orchestrator of comments 216055 and 3389 (hub)'}. Neither its
comment nor a `scheduled` event is a notify kind, and its orchestrator was a
dormant hub Desktop chat (tui notify rows only; no live session), so nothing
ever reached it. Earlier asks on the same card did wake it, because they were
`blocked` events, which the unloaded sweeper turns into a turn.

Root cause: the board had no producer kind for "my orchestrator must answer".
The awaiting guard refuses waits on David and agent walls, but an orchestrator
decision labelled `external` passed as a vendor wait with nobody to notify.

- kanban_awaiting: new awaiting kind `chat` (why = the question). Refused with
  `no_chat_subscriber` when no chat subscribes to the card. An `external` or
  inferred wait whose text waits on the owning/origin orchestrator is recorded
  as `chat` (reclassified_from), not refused.
- kanban_decision_ask: both park paths (schedule, timed block) append
  `decision_requested` in the park transaction.
- `decision_requested` is a gateway wake kind with a formatter and i18n key,
  a tui notify kind with a formatter (so the live poller and the unloaded
  sweeper deliver it, waking a dormant chat), and a scheduled-premise fold kind.
- Tool schema and CLI --awaiting help document the kind.

Tests: the live payload through the agent kanban_schedule tool, kanban_block
kind=time and CLI `hermes kanban schedule`; no-subscriber refusal; declared and
inferred chat waits; vendor waits and past citations unchanged; notify wiring.
9 of 11 fail on the parent (the 2 controls pass on both). 29 neighbouring
files, 487 tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
